Key Concepts & Stream Methods

Stream Creation: Converting arrays or lists into streams using Collection.stream() or Stream.of().

Filtering (filter): Selecting elements that satisfy a specific boolean condition (Predicate).

Data Transformation (map): Transforming each element into another value or type using a function.

Terminal Operations:

collect(Collectors.toList()): Accumulating elements into a collection.

reduce() / sum() / count() / average(): Reducing stream values down to a single result.

findFirst() / findAny(): Retrieving matching elements wrapped in an Optional.

forEach(): Iterating through stream elements.